  "question": {
    "text": "The area enclosed by the closed curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> given by the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>.&nbsp;Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> be the points of intersection of the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis. If normals at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> on the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> intersect <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> respectively, then the length of the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
